# All sessions, all repos

Standing operator ruling: **every** Cursor session (local and Cloud) and **every** product repo (existing and new) operates under JHD discipline. No exceptions for “quick Cloud fixes.”

## Existing repos
Must carry committed Cloud-portable discipline:
- `AGENTS.md`
- `.cursor/rules/` from plugin SoT `rules/` (invariants, routing, cloud-first, operator-voice, all-sessions) plus product overlay when applicable

Sync with `scripts/sync-discipline-into-product.sh <path> <kind>` (Mac) whenever `rules/` or templates change. Commit inside each product repo.

## New repos
Before the first agent session (local or Cloud):
1. Run `scripts/sync-discipline-into-product.sh <path> product` (or the matching kind from `config/jhd-repos.json`).
2. Commit `AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/rules/`.
3. Add the GitHub remote to the Cursor **Environment** alongside `jhd-cursor-discipline`.

## Every session
- Wrong-repo Cloud/local session → stop; open/start the correct product-repo session.
- Missing in-repo rules on Cloud → treat as incomplete setup; sync/commit before claiming discipline is active.
- Discipline-only workspace is for plugin maintenance — never for Capture/portfolio/product implementation.
- Vault absent on Cloud → say so; still follow in-repo rules.

## Cursor Environment (fleet)
Must include **`jhd-cursor-discipline` plus every active product remote** the operator ships. New product remote → add to Environment the same day.
